    <div class="eg-section-head"><span class="eg-eyebrow">Choose the layer deliberately</span><h2>A clear contract has a clear scope.</h2><p>EZGraph fits TypeScript applications with guided stages and explicit application policy. Assess its execution and persistence conventions against your requirements.</p></div>
    <div class="eg-fit"><div><h3>A useful fit when…</h3><p>You are building guided conversations, structured extraction, or reviewed tasks, and want a common way to organize nodes, histories, model policy, recovery, and sessions across them.</p></div><div><h3>Check the fit when…</h3><p>Your design depends on native token streaming, arbitrary checkpoint continuation, or unrestricted LangGraph topology. The current default is request/response turns, a constrained graph facade, and application session snapshots.</p></div></div>
